                    children:
                      shut_off:
                        block: period
                        description: keyword for activating well shut off capability.  Subsequent values
                          define the minimum and maximum pumping rate that a well must exceed to shutoff
                          or reactivate a well, respectively, during a stress period. SHUT_OFF is only applied
                          to injection wells (RATE$<0$) and if HEAD_LIMIT is specified (not set to `OFF').  If
                          HEAD_LIMIT is specified, SHUT_OFF can be deactivated by specifying a minimum value
                          equal to zero. The SHUT_OFF option is based on the SHUT_OFF functionality available
                          in the MNW2~citep{konikow2009} package for MODFLOW-2005. The SHUT_OFF option has
                          been included to facilitate backward compatibility with previous versions of MODFLOW
                          but use of the RATE_SCALING option instead of the SHUT_OFF option is recommended.
                          By default, SHUT_OFF is not used.
                        reader: urword
                        longname: shut off well
                        type: keyword
                      minrate:
                        block: period
                        description: is the minimum rate that a well must exceed to shutoff a well during
